# Accounts — {{PROJECT}}

> This file is yours (project-owned). It is the **customer/account hub** — one
> entry per account, and the **current-customers registry** (the accounts with
> `status: active`). `/account` creates and updates entries and flips status.
> Read `.claude/crm-rules.md` for the records + the won → active link;
> `.claude/crm-gate.md` for this business's customer-status and churn
> definitions.

> **crm owns this registry.** If a split business-ops module
> (`rasa.module.field-log`, `invoices`, `contracts`) is co-mounted, it joins
> to THIS file by `@acct-<slug>`. Do not seed a second accounts registry.

**Status:** `prospect → active → churned`. **`active` = a current customer.**
A lead reaching `won` flips its account to `active` (set `since` to the win
date). Never delete a churned account — flip its status; the history is data.

**Legend** — `@acct-<slug>` (the handle + shared join spine) ·
`status: prospect | active | churned` · `contacts:` a list of `CON-NNN`
(join to `crm/CONTACTS.md`). Grouped by status, **active (current customers)
first**.

